Four declarations of a package nothing outside can import, each the subject of a kind
outside the unused-declaration group: an interface nothing names as a type, a method
of a live interface no call site invokes through it, a member of an enumerated type
nothing names, and the type parameter of a live exported function that neither its
signature nor its body names. Beside them sits an exported function nothing
references, which is the one declaration the unreachable-export kind reports. Every
one of the five is exported and every one sits under an internal tree, so the
unreachable-export kind would take all five if the kinds did not agree on which code
reports what.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27.0
-- main.go --
package main

import "example.com/app/internal/api"

func main() {
	var store api.Store = api.Filesystem{}
	println(store.Read(), api.Convert[int](1))
}
-- internal/api/api.go --
package api

// Reader is an interface nothing names as a type.
type Reader interface {
	Read() string
}

// Store is named as a type, and Flush is never invoked through it.
type Store interface {
	Read() string
	Flush() error
}

// Filesystem implements Store.
type Filesystem struct{}

// Read answers the contents.
func (Filesystem) Read() string { return "" }

// Flush writes what is held.
func (Filesystem) Flush() error { return nil }

// Level is how loudly the package reports, and nothing names Quiet.
type Level int

// The levels, of which only Loud is named.
const (
	Loud Level = iota
	Quiet
)

// Convert names its type parameter in neither its signature nor its body.
func Convert[T any](n int) int { return n + int(Loud) }

// Forgotten is referenced by nothing.
func Forgotten() int { return 3 }
